  <TabItem label="7. Lifecycle and view">

The hook dispatches a typed thunk, keeps its abortable handle in a ref, and cancels it during cleanup. Refetch cancels the previous request for this screen.

### `src/features/user/presentation/hooks/useUserProfile.ts`

```typescript
import { useCallback, useEffect, useRef } from 'react';
import { useAppDispatch, useAppSelector } from '../../../../app/hooks';
import { loadUserProfile, profileRemoved, selectProfile } from '../state/profileSlice';

export function useUserProfile(screenKey: string, userId: string, isActive: boolean) {
  const dispatch = useAppDispatch();
  const state = useAppSelector((root) => selectProfile(root, screenKey));
  type Request = ReturnType<ReturnType<typeof loadUserProfile>>;
  const active = useRef<Request | null>(null);

  const refresh = useCallback(() => {
    if (!isActive) return;
    active.current?.abort();
    active.current = dispatch(loadUserProfile({ screenKey, userId }));
  }, [dispatch, screenKey, userId, isActive]);

  useEffect(() => {
    refresh();
    return () => {
      active.current?.abort();
      active.current = null;
    };
  }, [refresh]);

  useEffect(() => () => {
    dispatch(profileRemoved(screenKey));
  }, [dispatch, screenKey]);

  return { state, refresh };
}
```

<Aside type="tip" title="Hint · mounted does not always mean visible">
React Navigation screens can remain mounted after losing focus. The host supplies `isActive` from its navigation-focus and application-lifecycle policy. Losing activity cancels screen work; becoming active loads again. Cleanup removes the screen entry when its owning screen is unmounted or its key changes. React Strict Mode may run an extra setup/cleanup cycle in development; the abort and request-ID guards handle that lifecycle.
</Aside>

The promise returned by dispatching an async thunk resolves to a lifecycle action. Use `.unwrap()` only when a caller needs success/failure control flow, and catch its rejection. This screen renders the result from Redux state, so it does not need `.unwrap()`.

