The view uses `react-native-safe-area-context`; the app must supply its `SafeAreaProvider`. Coordinate safe-area edges with the host navigator to avoid duplicate insets. Core React Native's legacy `SafeAreaView` is deprecated; see the [React Native reference](https://reactnative.dev/docs/SafeAreaView).

Replace the sample palette and copy with enterprise theme tokens and localized resources. Keep the scrollable layout, disabled/busy semantics, accessible labels, and text scaling. Test announcements on both platforms; an Android live-region prop alone does not establish equivalent iOS VoiceOver behavior.

Memoization is optional. Use `memo`, `useCallback`, or memoized selectors when reference stability or measured rendering cost warrants them. Inline callbacks do not inherently cause “bridge flooding,” and `memo` does not guarantee a performance improvement.

